From: Wine upstream contributors (see commit list)
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Accept no-error and non-forward-compatible core context requests.

Behaviour adapted from WineHQ commits 632068bd35 and af79eeb0d0 (wine-11.19,
both by Rémi Bernon), which move wglCreateContextAttribsARB parsing into
win32u. That refactor does not apply to this base; Runeon contributors
carried only its effect on these two checks into the base's attribute loop.

win32u advertises WGL_ARB_create_context_no_error for every driver, and an
SDL 2.0.16 application was observed adding WGL_CONTEXT_OPENGL_NO_ERROR_ARB
to its 3.2 core request when it saw that extension. macdrv_context_create()
treated the attribute as unknown and failed with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER.
CGL has no no-error mode, so the attribute is now accepted and ignored, as
upstream does.

macdrv_context_create() also refused 3.2-4.1 core requests that did not set
WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB. macOS core contexts have no
deprecated functionality, so the result is what a forward-compatible request
gets; macOS cannot offer the wider non-forward-compatible core context that
Windows drivers may. Upstream no longer requires the flag either.

Not taken from upstream: its handling of legacy versions (3.0 without flags,
3.1, and 1.x/2.x with the forward-compatible bit), of an explicit zero
profile mask and of 3.2+ compatibility profiles, and its error code for a
version above the host maximum. Those requests keep their base results.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
index 8c7b3fe..8f24ef5 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -2152,6 +2152,13 @@ static BOOL macdrv_context_create(int format, void *shared, const int *attrib_li
                 profile = value;
                 break;
 
+            case WGL_CONTEXT_OPENGL_NO_ERROR_ARB:
+                /* CGL has no no-error mode, and a context that still reports
+                 * errors is a valid answer to the request. */
+                if (value)
+                    WARN("WGL_CONTEXT_OPENGL_NO_ERROR_ARB ignored\n");
+                break;
+
             default:
                 WARN("Unknown attribute %s.\n", debugstr_attrib(attr, value));
                 RtlSetLastWin32Error(ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER);
@@ -2171,12 +2178,8 @@ static BOOL macdrv_context_create(int format, void *shared, const int *attrib_li
                 flags |= WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB;
         }
 
-        if (!(flags & WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB))
-        {
-            WARN("OS X only supports forward-compatible 3.2+ contexts\n");
-            RtlSetLastWin32Error(ERROR_INVALID_VERSION_ARB);
-            return FALSE;
-        }
+        /* A core profile context has no deprecated functionality, so it is
+         * what a forward-compatible one would be; the flag is not required. */
         if (profile != WGL_CONTEXT_CORE_PROFILE_BIT_ARB)
         {
             WARN("Compatibility profiles for GL version >= 3.2 not supported\n");
